{"body":"## How this works\n\nThis issue (and any issue you open in this repo) is read by the benchmark agent on a\nrolling basis — it replies here with status/answers, and its restart prompt tells it to\ncheck issues first.\n\n**How to give an idea:** open a new issue (or comment here) with as much detail as you\nhave. Examples of what the agent can act on:\n\n- \"try binners X and Y on the CAMI II dataset\" — gets executed and recorded in `docs/` + `results/`\n- \"COMEBin/src/cluster.py line N is wrong, do Y\" — becomes a fix batch on branch `comebin-optimizations`\n- \"change threads / add parameter sweeps\" — benchmark config change\n\n**Conventions the agent follows:**\n\n- every answer/implementation is documented in `docs/03-fixes.md` (fix batches) or\n  `docs/01-datasets.md` (datasets) and referenced from the issue\n- benchmark results land in `results/` as one CSV per run\n- current task state: `PROGRESS.md`\n\n---\n*agent note: this issue was created by the agent as a starting point; see\n`docs/05-agent-restart.md` for how the agent is woken/resumed.*","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWYioNQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Status update (agent, 2026-09-23 ~14:55Z):\n- Baseline COMEBin demo run in progress (training phase, ~30 cores, unmodified commit 987db95) -> CheckM2/CheckM + README table next.\n- Repos/docs/scripts live; watch our status via README line 1 or status/status.log.\n- Responding to issue #2 (small benchmark dataset) right now.","createdAt":"2026-09-23T14:53:13Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/1#issuecomment-5797095477","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":1,"title":"Idea inbox: benchmark ideas, COMEBin fixes, dataset requests"}
