{"body":"The big benchmark takes too long, please use a human based benchmark set from cami that is like 1/6 the of the big one, also try to find a tool dataset combi that is even smaller then the small dataset - the smallest still possible, needs to be functional an create bins though","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWzHYAQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Triage (agent, 2026-09-25 01:10 UTC) — both directives accepted, plan below.\n\n**Context first:** the run you were waiting on finished while the session was down — `fix_v11_20260924` completed 2026-09-24 17:29 UTC, exit 0, 71 bins, wall **24,741 s (6.9 h)**, and it stopped early at epoch 184/200 because upstream v1.1.0 `run_comebin.sh` passes `--earlystop` (Top-1 > 99 % for 3 epochs). CheckM2 is done (71 bins), CheckM v1 is running now. So yes — ~7 h per large run is way too slow for iteration, agreed.\n\n### 1. Human CAMI set at ~1/6 the size of the big one\n- \"Big\" = the full demo: **29,434 contigs / 6.9 h** → target ≈ **4,900 contigs**, expected wall time ≈ 1–1.5 h per run.\n- Source (docs/08): CAMI II human host-associated — *Multisample Human Microbiome Project* (DOI 10.4126/frl01-006425518) or *Toy Human Microbiome* (per-body-site download via camiClient, e.g. `CAMI_Gastrointestinal_tract`).\n- Steps: download one human sample within the ≤30 GB budget → subset the assembly to the ~4,900 longest contigs → map that sample's reads to the subset with `bwa mem` → record md5/provenance in `docs/01` → run `run_comebin_fix.sh` + `run_eval.sh` and report CheckM2/CheckM v1 next to the baseline row.\n- If you meant 1/6 by **bytes/read count** instead of contigs, say so and I'll size the subset by that metric instead.\n\n### 2. Smallest possible tool + dataset combo that still works\n- Current smallest: `comebin_small` = 300 contigs / 94 MB / 122 s (30 epochs) → 3 non-empty bins.\n- I'll step down (300 → 200 → 150 → 100 → 50 …) and keep the **smallest** combo that (a) trains without the zero-batch crash and (b) produces **≥ 1 non-empty bin**, verified end-to-end by `scripts/run_small_test.sh` + CheckM2/CheckM. Every attempt is logged under `runs/`, and the chosen size + measured wall time get added to `docs/08`.\n\nOrder of work: finish the `fix_v11` evaluation and publish its row → build the tiny set (fast) → build the ~1/6 human set (download). I'll report actual sizes and timings here as each lands.\n","createdAt":"2026-09-25T01:07:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/18#issuecomment-5824960513","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWznCiQ","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Smallest-functional-dataset stepping: first two results are in.\n\n- `tiny_test_n100` (100 contigs): **fails** — exit 1, 0 bins (below the training floor).\n- `tiny_test_n101` (101 contigs): **passes end-to-end** — exit 0, wall 85 s (30 epochs), 1 non-empty bin; CheckM2 rc 0 (44 s): 63.89% completeness / 9.05% contamination (MQ 1); CheckM v1 rc 0 (114 s): 46.58% / 6.35%. Row: `results/tiny_test_n101.csv`, per-bin + plots auto-regenerated.\n\nSo the current floor is **101 contigs / ~85 s** — about 30% smaller and faster than `comebin_small` (300 contigs / 122 s). Next: the ~1/6 human host-associated set per the plan above; sizes and timings reported here as they land.","createdAt":"2026-09-25T02:04:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/18#issuecomment-5825479305","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWzw1-g","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Human host-associated set (#18b) — input built, run launched.\n\n**Dataset** (`/vol/data/datasets/cami_II_human/human_sample0_input`, built by `scripts/prep_cami2_human.sh 4900`):\n- Source: CAMI II Toy Human Microbiome `gastrooral/sample_0` (frl:6425518), 9,738,621,091 B, md5 `60e04c041c38ea168af03fc55dff15d6` verified.\n- Contigs: top **4,900 longest** GSA contigs (of 68,417) → **166,008,681 bp**, min 4,733 / max 5,287,944, N50 1,464,728 — ≈ 1/6 of the demo set (29,434 contigs / 1.0 Gbp) as requested.\n- Reads: the per-OTU `bam/OTU_*.bam` files are unusable for a co-assembly run (each covers one genome), so **all 10.6 GB of interleaved paired reads were re-mapped** with `bwa mem -p -t 32` → `bamfiles/human.bam` (4.74 GB, indexed; md5 `c48e4caa94c3c11640ba6ed4b96ab0e4`).\n\n**Run:** `runs/human_v11_20260925` launched 02:17 UTC with the fix source (COMEBin-v11 @ `95f5ea8`), seed 42, 32 threads, registered with the watchdog (`.active_run`). Augmentation already reports `assembly_contigs=4900, retained_contigs=4900, views=6`. Target wall ≈ 1 h vs 6.9 h for the demo set; results (CheckM2 + CheckM v1, aggregate CSV, per-bin tables) will be posted here and in `docs/11-run-results.md` when it finishes.","createdAt":"2026-09-25T02:23:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/18#issuecomment-5825639930","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABW0iiwg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Human host-associated set (#18b) — **run complete + evaluated**.\n\n**Run** `human_v11_20260925` (2026-09-25 02:17 → 03:39 UTC, wall **4,912 s ≈ 1.37 h** vs 6.9 h on the ≤ 1/6-larger demo): exit 0, **200/200 epochs** (no early-stop; Top-1 plateaued ≈ 96%), 120/120 Leiden clustering → **107 non-empty bins** on the 4,900-contig / 166 Mbp set (top-4900-longest contigs of CAMI II Toy Human Microbiome `gastrooral/sample_0`, reads re-mapped with `bwa mem`).\n\n**Quality** (`scripts/run_eval.sh`, fix source `95f5ea8`, seed 42):\n- **CheckM2** (wall 193 s): mean completeness **35.31 %**, contamination **5.13 %** → **HQ 20 / MQ 29** (≥90 & ≤5 / ≥50 & ≤10).\n- **CheckM v1** (wall 686 s): mean completeness **32.64 %**, contamination **4.65 %** → **HQ 21 / MQ 29**.\n- Top bins approximate complete genomes and both tools agree: bin0 100 %/0.45 %, bin1 100 %/0.20 %, bin2 100 %/0.03 % (CheckM2) with CheckM v1 100 %/0.0 %.\n\n**Highlight:** first dataset in this benchmark with substantial HQ recovery — 20–21 near-complete bins vs 1 (CheckM2) / 0 (CheckM v1) on the full demo, and more total bins (107 vs 60–71) at ~1/5 the wall time. Artifacts: [`results/human_v11_20260925.csv`](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/results/human_v11_20260925.csv), per-bin table `runs/human_v11_20260925/per_bin_results.csv`, `docs/11-run-results.md` row added.\n\nIssues #18a (tiny floor = 101 contigs) and #18b (human ~1/6) are now both measured. Next per plan: **CAMI II marine sample_0** (~1/6 set) → baseline + fix runs, then CAMI III.","createdAt":"2026-09-25T03:59:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/18#issuecomment-5826454210","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABW0kY2g","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Closed by automation — addressed: issue #18 complete: smallest functional dataset found and measured (floor = 101 contigs: tiny_test_n100 fails with HNSW k=101>N, tiny_test_n101 passes end-to-end, results/tiny_test_n101.csv) AND CAMI II human host-associated ~1/6 set built (4,900 contigs/166 Mbp, reads re-mapped), benchmarked (runs/human_v11_20260925: exit 0, 4,912 s, 107 bins, CheckM2 35.31/5.13 HQ20/MQ29, CheckM v1 32.64/4.65 HQ","createdAt":"2026-09-25T04:03:09Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/18#issuecomment-5826484442","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":18