{'id': 'IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABW3TZ8A', 'author': {'login': 'paulzierep'}, 'authorAssociation': 'OWNER', 'body': "Thanks for the feedback! Regarding the request for stats tables under the bar plots: the per-run bar charts () already show CheckM2 + CheckM v1 completeness and contamination per bin as bar groups. The all-runs comparison scatter () and per-dataset subplot () provide cross-run and same-dataset comparisons. The aggregate run stats (completeness, contamination, #bins) are recorded in  and mirrored in the  Results section. If you're looking for a tabular display alongside the plots in the README, that would be a natural next step — the data is already available via  output, just not rendered as a table in the markdown. Would you like me to explore adding a table summary to the README Results section, or were you thinking of something more specific?", 'createdAt': '2026-09-25T08:28:10Z', 'includesCreatedEdit': False, 'isMinimized': False, 'minimizedReason': '', 'reactionGroups': [], 'url': 'https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/12#issuecomment-5829351920', 'viewerDidAuthor': True}
{'id': 'IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABW3dIYA', 'author': {'login': 'paulzierep'}, 'authorAssociation': 'OWNER', 'body': "Regarding continuous updating of the same Zenodo record: the current setup (record 22935025) already stores the small benchmark dataset with MIT license and expanded metadata. The Zenodo API supports updating record metadata in-place, so new benchmark datasets (medium, CAMI II marine, CAMI III) can be added to the same record by creating a new deposition version or updating the existing record's files. The key is that the record DOI remains the same, so all benchmark data accumulates under one DOI. I will set up a workflow for adding new datasets to the existing record via the manifest infrastructure documented in docs/10-data-preservation.md. Each new dataset (medium, CAMI II marine, CAMI III) will be packaged with its manifest, and the record will be updated via the Zenodo API.\n\nCurrent datasets under this DOI: comebin_small (94 MB, MIT license, 10.5281/zenodo.22935025). Next: medium_v11_20260924 (3,000 contigs, 421 MB), marine_v11_20260925 (cami2 mode, ~10 GB), and CAMI III (planned, ≤30 GB).\n\nThe manifest infrastructure (scripts/make_release_manifest.py, docs/10-data-preservation.md) already provides the provenance framework — each dataset package includes SHA-256/size manifests, and the record metadata can be updated in-place via the API.", 'createdAt': '2026-09-25T08:41:17Z', 'includesCreatedEdit': False, 'isMinimized': False, 'minimizedReason': '', 'reactionGroups': [], 'url': 'https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/12#issuecomment-5829511264', 'viewerDidAuthor': True}
