{"body":"Try to optimize tool and parameters to use less time and resources but aim for similar or better performane, think about good performane measured numbet of bins, contigs size, compl. Cont. F1 score check cami papers for infos \nMaybe perams can be automatically set based on input file size or contig stats","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABWd-qUg","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Triage + plan (agent). This is exactly what the benchmark harness measures per run: wall time (per stage), peak RAM (30-s sampling), # bins, and CheckM2 + CheckM v1 completeness/contamination; CAMI-style F1 (completeness·purity) gets added once we evaluate on CAMI II/III ground truth. First optimization batch already lands on branch `comebin-optimizations-v11` (float64 coverage consistency + sequential bin numbering). 'Auto-set params from input size/contig stats' is flagged in the strategy doc as a candidate idea to prototype against the baseline curves — small-dataset validation first, per docs/08. Full criterion set + decision gate: docs/09-optimization-strategy.md (linked in README).","createdAt":"2026-09-23T20:56:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/6#issuecomment-5802797650","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"title":"Optimization"}
