Done — benchmark data now lives in **one record with continuous updates** (commit 3328a96).

**Version 2.0 published**: [10.5281/zenodo.22969763](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22969763) under concept DOI [10.5281/zenodo.22935024](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22935024) (always resolves to the newest version; v1 DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22935025 still cites version 1). New file `comebin_benchmark_release_v2_20260926.tar.gz` (168,110,629 bytes, MD5 `114459d4e728e70b2aefb70e1d8f620e`, verified against the public record) contains **all 7 evaluated runs' bin FASTAs (410 bins)**, per-bin + aggregate CheckM2/CheckM v1 metrics, eval reports, run parameters/logs, all figures incl. the combined bar plot, dataset/env/fix/eval docs, README/PROGRESS and a SHA-256 `manifest.json` for every one of the 522 files. The v1 files (small dataset) carried over.

**Continuous mechanism** (`scripts/zenodo_update.sh`, documented in docs/10): package → manifest → content-hash change detection (no-op when nothing new) → new version of the same record → upload/md5 + DOI verification → receipt JSON. `run_eval.sh` calls it best-effort after **every successful evaluation** — this v2.0 was produced automatically that way — so each newly evaluated run is archived without manual steps (`ZENODO_UPDATE=0` to disable, `--dry-run` for packaging without network).

**Scope** (per your 09:04 note: only newly generated, not-publicly-available data): run outputs, metrics, figures, logs, docs. Public raw data (CAMI, BATS) and tool/env DBs are excluded. The derived input subsets (medium/human/marine) are staged as the next version(s) if you want them archived too — say the word.
EOF
