=== 34ea532 stat ===
commit 34ea5329180e288167c5c0f1413cfc8c5067d316
Author: paulzierep <paulzierep@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Sep 26 02:10:43 2026 +0000

    Fix reporting/Zenodo auto-update pipeline that was never actually deployed
    
    The #12 and #8 delivery comments claimed the combined bar plot and the
    continuous Zenodo version were regenerated automatically after every
    evaluated run. That was true in the repo but false in the installed
    runtime, and two defects would have kept it false:
    
    - make_combined_bar_plot.py and zenodo_update.sh were never installed to
      /vol/data/benchmark/bin, and bin/run_eval.sh was the pre-feature version,
      so the next evaluation would have produced neither figure nor Zenodo version.
    - Every reporting helper resolved the repo as dirname(script)/.., which is
      the benchmark data dir rather than the repo when invoked from bin/ (its
      helpers are called via $(dirname $0)). Figures/CSVs/tables would have been
      written outside git and README, and zenodo_update.sh would have packaged an
      incomplete release with no docs/, status/ or README.md. A stale artifact from
      this bug (bench-root results/small_test_v4.csv, superseded CheckM v1 values)
