19:## Run history — what happened and what's next
21:Fifteen COMEBin-executing attempts have been recorded: eight terminal failures and seven completed runs. The baseline rerun, small functional gate, medium derivative, large fix run, the 101-contig tiny floor run, the CAMI II human ~1/6 run, and the CAMI II marine ~1/6 run now have verified bin artifacts and CheckM2/CheckM outputs. Run links point to tracked evidence mirrors; the status banner at the top is authoritative for any active run.
23:### COMEBin-executing attempts
37:| [`fix_v11_20260924`](../runs/fix_v11_20260924/comebin_run.log) — 2026-09-24 10:37:15 → 17:29:36 | [95f5ea8](https://github.com/paulzierep/COMEBin/commit/95f5ea820f9a4e76f5c2911c0b5ed507ab67b015) | **✅ Complete** (exit 0, wall 24,741 s). Stopped early at **epoch 184/200** because upstream v1.1.0 `run_comebin.sh` passes `--earlystop` (Top-1 > 99% for 3 epochs: 99.10 → 99.22 → 99.04%), then clustering completed normally (120/120 Leiden) → **71 non-empty bins**. CheckM2: 24.38% / 3.78% (HQ 1, MQ 6). CheckM v1: 21.62% / 5.18% (HQ 0, MQ 8). Versus the baseline on the same data: +1.7% wall time, +11 bins, −0.63 pp completeness, +0.80 pp contamination. | Evaluation done with `scripts/run_eval.sh` (CheckM2 71 s, CheckM v1 398 s); see the [aggregate CSV](../results/fix_v11_20260924.csv) and [per-bin table](../runs/fix_v11_20260924/per_bin_results.csv). Next: issue #18 datasets (tiny + CAMI human ~1/6). |
39:| [`tiny_test_n101`](../runs/tiny_test_n101/comebin_run.log) — 2026-09-25 01:46:33 → 01:47:58 (85 s) | [c8f22e4](https://github.com/paulzierep/COMEBin/commit/c8f22e4935a66a0fd58b794489a9021671b15437) | **✅ Complete.** 101 contigs (issue #18 tiny floor), 30/30 epochs, exit 0, **1 non-empty bin**. CheckM2: 63.89% / 9.05% (MQ 1). CheckM v1: 46.58% / 6.35%. | Smallest passing dataset verified; see [`results/tiny_test_n101.csv`](../results/tiny_test_n101.csv). CAMI-II human ~1/6 set is next (issue #18). |
40:| [`human_v11_20260925`](../runs/human_v11_20260925/comebin_run.log) — 2026-09-25 02:17:20 → 03:39:12 (4,912 s = 82 min, 5× faster than the 6.9 h demo run) | [95f5ea8](https://github.com/paulzierep/COMEBin/commit/95f5ea820f9a4e76f5c2911c0b5ed507ab67b015) | **✅ Complete** (exit 0). Issue #18b human host-associated set: top-4,900-longest contigs of CAMI II Toy Human Microbiome `gastrooral/sample_0` (166 Mbp, ~1/6 demo), all 10.6 GB reads re-mapped `bwa mem -p` → `bamfiles/human.bam` (`scripts/prep_cami2_human.sh 4900`). 200/200 epochs (final Top-1 95.94%, no early stop), 120/120 Leiden → **107 non-empty bins**. CheckM2: 35.31% / 5.13% (HQ 20, MQ 29). CheckM v1: 32.64% / 4.65% (HQ 21, MQ 29). First dataset in the benchmark with substantial HQ recovery (top bins ≈ 100% / ≤ 0.45% under both tools). | Evaluation via `scripts/run_eval.sh` (CheckM2 rc 0 / 193 s, CheckM v1 rc 0 / 686 s); [aggregate CSV](../results/human_v11_20260925.csv), [per-bin table](../runs/human_v11_20260925/per_bin_results.csv). Coverage used 1 worker (single BAM) — same setup for the marine set. Next: CAMI II marine sample_0 (~1/6) run, then CAMI III. |
