### CAMI III toy human gut — run complete (2026-09-26)

Newest dataset results, per the run-logging protocol (full history: [docs/11-run-results.md](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/docs/11-run-results.md)).

**`cami3_v11_20260926_rerun`** — CAMI III toy human gut, top-5,000 pooled-GSA contigs (1.1 Gbp, both samples' coverage BAMs), `MODE=cami3`, seed 42, 32 threads, branch `comebin-optimizations-v11` (`95f5ea8`):

| metric | value |
|---|---|
| wall time / peak RAM | **5,392 s (90 min)** / 10.37 GB |
| training | 200/200 epochs (final Top-1 74.95 %, no early stop), Leiden 120/120 |
| bins | **492** non-empty |
| CheckM2 | **35.97 % / 11.42 %** (HQ 53, MQ 112) |
| CheckM v1 | **32.46 % / 13.38 %** (HQ 54, MQ 100) |

Most bins and most HQ/MQ bins of any run so far (marine remains best mean quality: 152 bins @ 50.60/4.10). CAMI III carries the highest mean contamination of the benchmark — strain-rich toy gut, where strain heterogeneity scores as contamination. Row CSV: [results/cami3_v11_20260926_rerun.csv](https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/blob/main/results/cami3_v11_20260926_rerun.csv).

**Two operational findings relevant to this issue:**

1. **ENOSPC first attempt** (`cami3_v11_20260926`, exit 1 @ 6,677 s, 0 bins) was *not* a binning bug: prep-leftover downloads (13.8 GB in `/tmp`) had filled `/` to 100 %, which silently poisoned CheckM's marker tables (21 hmmfetch fatals) → final selection died on `KeyError: '110'`. Leftovers verified already staged in the dataset, deleted (`/` 100 → 28 %), and a deterministic rerun from a fresh dir completed cleanly — epoch-99 loss/accuracy bit-identical to attempt 1 (seed-42 replay confirmed). Lesson for the harness: pre-flight a free-disk check (≥ ~20 GB) before launching; the run fails *late* (at get_result) when the disk is short, not early.
2. **CheckM2 thread race at 492 bins**: `checkm2 predict --threads 32` failed gene-calling (`cannot create protein_files/*.gff.NN` → *List of protein files does not match internal reference*); a 16-thread retry into a fresh output dir succeeded (1,137 s, failed attempt preserved as `eval/checkm2.incomplete.*`). For ≥ ~500 bins, cap CheckM2 at 16 threads.

**Deliverables:** docs/11 rows (summary + both attempts), README bullet, per-bin table/plots, and **Zenodo v3** published — [10.5281/zenodo.22973575](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22973575) (520 MB incl. the 492 new bins per #8; concept DOI unchanged).
EOF
