{"body":"make sure to use a seed for all runs, so runs re reproducible","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOUndL2c8AAAABXF_E3Q","author":{"login":"paulzierep"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Good point on seeds for reproducibility. The project already uses seed 42 for COMEBin runs (as seen in run_meta.txt across benchmarks), and the optimization fix batches commit / on the  branch addressed sklearn KMeans compatibility. For full reproducibility, we should also ensure Python/RNG states are seeded at the start of each run (numpy, PyTorch, and the Leiden optimizer). This would complement the existing seed=42 approach and make across-run comparisons more reliable.","createdAt":"2026-09-26T08:51:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/paulzierep/metagenomic-binning-benchmark/issues/21#issuecomment-5844747485","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"number":21,"title":"use a seed for all runs"}
